        a                              ecrm:E22_Man-Made_Object ;
        rdfs:comment                   "Pair of woman’s sleeves, removed from a gown or bodice, made of white silk satin and embroidered with purple silk floss and silver filé, in a pattern of scrolling stems and floral motifs, with couching, satin stitch and French knots. The sleeves are lined with linen and edged with a fringe of white silk and silver filé."@en , "Pair of woman's sleeves, 1700c, French; White silk satin, embroidered with purple silk and silver thread"@en ;
